{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["And the one who carries — moves it from its place even though he did not touch it; but if a carcass was loaded on his shoulder and he did not touch it and it did not move from its place, he is not impure. And so we learned in tractate Zavim. And even a corpse lying on a bed, with paper beneath it that separates between the corpse and the utensils beneath it — they are pure, for a corpse imparts impurity only by carrying, which is moving. And so we learned there. And in the Jerusalem Targum it is translated: 'one who carries' — 'moves.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:40.241778137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}